<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
  <%#
    The other half of what `shadcn--avatar` is for: a picture that fails leaves
    the initials showing rather than a broken-image icon. The source is a data
    URI that cannot decode, so the failure needs nothing from the network.

    Its own preview rather than a sixth avatar on `default`, because a picture
    that fails writes to the browser console whichever way it is broken — a
    404, a bad URL, a truncated file — and `smoke_spec` visits every family's
    `default` and expects its console silent. Here it is read by the snapshot
    and the accessibility specs, neither of which listens.
  %>
  <%= render(Shadcn::Avatar::Component.new) do |a| %>
    <% a.with_image(src: "data:image/png;base64,not-a-png", alt: "Grace Hopper") %>
    <% a.with_fallback { "GH" } %>
  <% end %>
</div>
